# Copy style

User-facing copy uses **closed slashes**, **closed em dashes**, and **spaced workflow arrows**. Do not use spaced slashes, spaced em dashes, or closed arrows.

```
✅ Harbor & Co/SupportFlow
✅ Laravel/Livewire
✅ PostgreSQL/pgvector
✅ live models—not canned scripts
✅ High (88%)—model-estimated
✅ (similarity 0.31)—measured
✅ Warranty claim—snapped trekking pole
✅ Customer → submit a fictional ticket → keep the status page open.

Hi Jamie,

Reply text...

Best,
Alex Rivera
Harbor & Co Support

❌ Harbor & Co / SupportFlow
❌ Laravel / Livewire
❌ live models — not canned scripts
❌ High (88%) — model-estimated
❌ Hi Jamie—unused items can be returned
❌ Hi Jamie — unused items can be returned
❌ Customer→submit
```

- Compound product, stack, and policy names take a closed slash (`Shipping/returns`, `Tokens in/out`).
- An em dash joins words with no spaces (`word—word`). Do not put a newline that collapses to a space before or after the dash in HTML.
- Customer-facing suggested replies put exactly one personalized greeting on its own line (`Hi Jamie,`), then a blank line, then the body, then a blank line, then this three-line closing: `Best,` / `Alex Rivera` / `Harbor & Co Support`. Do not join the greeting to the body with an em dash. Do not emit a second `Hi,` greeting.
- Workflow steps keep a space on both sides of `→`.
- Do not replace these with hyphens, en dashes, or pipes in UI copy.
- Leave code, URLs, arithmetic, and standalone placeholder dashes alone (`1 / ($k + $rank)`, `Missing usage shows as —.`).
